Export the renderer's own GPU release to embedders (ghostty_surface_release_gpu_resources).

At 683d8db the generic renderer frees a hidden surface's swap chain (render targets, font atlas textures, cell,
uniform and background-image buffers, custom shader textures) from setVisible(false), but only where it may touch
the GPU from the render thread. The OpenGL embedding of 0001 draws on the app thread inside the host's GL area
(must_draw_from_app_thread), so occlusion keeps all of it and the embedding API has no other way to free it. The
new call runs the renderer's releaseGpuResources on the app thread, with the surface's GL context current (the
host's job). The next drawFrame rebuilds the swap chain; the terminal and its visibility are not touched. It
takes only the renderer's draw mutex, never the terminal state mutex, so it needs no demand guard (0002).

